  "notes": "The transitive counterpart is {収|おさ}める (to put in, to store; to bring under control). The kanji {収|おさ}まる focuses on containment and resolution, while the homophone {治|おさ}まる focuses on governance or healing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {丸|まる}く{収|おさ}まる — to be resolved amicably\n- {怒|いか}りが{収|おさ}まる — anger subsides\n- {騒|さわ}ぎが{収|おさ}まる — commotion dies down\n- {予算|よさん}に{収|おさ}まる — to stay within budget\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {治|おさ}まる — to be governed; to heal, to be cured\n- {納|おさ}まる — to be delivered, to be paid",
